= 29–30 July 1974 — Geneva I concludes

At the conference, the airport question was being discussed, and the British were insisting that their formula be accepted. Güneş intervened:

“This conference must end. Mr. Callaghan, let us leave the airport question to the technicians and take it up at the second conference... If you accept this, I would like to speak privately with Mr. Mavros.”

Mehmet Ali Birand, 30 Sıcak Gün, PDF page 357 — English translation of the source excerpt.


- @historical: Conclude Geneva I and accept the declaration against further territorial expansion.
- @alternative: Prioritize joint verification of local positions and reciprocal adjustments under UN supervision.

